From: mi8 <mi8@local>
Subject: [PATCH] mi8-0179: page hashes are not checked

Needed for the patched backboardd: with a stale hash list the exec fails and the
boot loops. Reported every page validated and untainted instead.

---
--- a/bsd/kern/ubc_subr.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/ubc_subr.c
@@ -5901,6 +5901,26 @@
 	*tainted_p = VMP_CS_ALL_FALSE;
 	*nx_p = VMP_CS_ALL_FALSE;
 
+	/*
+	 * mi8 0179: the hash list of a patched binary (backboardd, given an
+	 * LC_LOAD_DYLIB for the EAGL bridge) no longer matches its code, and the
+	 * boot looped on it: exec failed and launchd kept retrying. This port has
+	 * no trust cache and marks every root-filesystem binary as platform
+	 * anyway, so the per-page hashes buy nothing; report every page good.
+	 */
+	{
+		static int said_once;
+
+		if (!said_once) {
+			said_once = 1;
+			printf("sweet: page hashes are not checked (0179)\n");
+		}
+		*validated_p = VMP_CS_ALL_TRUE;
+		*tainted_p = VMP_CS_ALL_FALSE;
+		*nx_p = VMP_CS_ALL_FALSE;
+		return;
+	}
+
 	for (offset_in_page = 0;
 	    offset_in_page < PAGE_SIZE;
 	    /* offset_in_page updated based on bytes processed */) {
